{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"35fe2271a2fa25730c46733e","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran%40microchip.com/","channels":["linux-arm-kernel"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran%40microchip.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v6 02/17] nvmem: add DEFINE_FREE for nvmem_cell_put cleanup","messages":{"20260815205238.6fbfb2f8@jic23-huawei":{"id":"20260815205238.6fbfb2f8@jic23-huawei","messageId":"20260815205238.6fbfb2f8@jic23-huawei","references":["20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com","20260806074024.531259-3-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260806074024.531259-3-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com","20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"],"author":{"name":"Jonathan Cameron","address":"jic23@kernel.org"},"sender":{"name":"linux-arm-kernel","address":"linux-arm-kernel-bounces@lists.infradead.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Varshini Rajendran","address":"varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"ehristev@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dlechner@baylibre.com"},{"name":"","address":"nuno.sa@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"andy@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"conor+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nicolas.ferre@microchip.com"},{"name":"","address":"alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com"},{"name":"","address":"claudiu.beznea@tuxon.dev"},{"name":"","address":"srini@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"marcelo.schmitt@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"radu.sabau@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"joshua.crofts1@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"jorge.marques@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"Jonathan.Santos@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"jishnu.prakash@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"duje@dujemihanovic.xyz"},{"name":"","address":"mazziesaccount@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-iio@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-15T19:52:38.000Z","iso":"2026-08-15T19:52:38.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v6 02/17] nvmem: add DEFINE_FREE for nvmem_cell_put cleanup","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","displayName":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:10:09 +0530\nVarshini Rajendran <varshini.rajendran@microchip.com> wrote:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Add cleanup.h helper for nvmem_cell_put() to enable automatic resource"},{"depth":1,"text":"cleanup using __free(nvmem_cell_put) annotation."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Use IS_ERR_OR_NULL() since nvmem_cell_get() can return error pointers,"},{"depth":1,"text":"and passing an ERR_PTR to nvmem_cell_put() would cause issues."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Varshini Rajendran <varshini.rajendran@microchip.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"}],"lineCount":8,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Srinivas, if you are happy with this header addition please could\nI have an Ack to take this through the IIO tree?  If it's useful\nfor other series, I can provide an immutable branch that you can\npull into the nvmem tree.  I'll probably spin one of those on rc1\nonce available anyway just in case someone else needs it later\nin the cycle."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"No huge rush - just good to keep this moving!"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Jonathan"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":" include/linux/nvmem-consumer.h | 3 +++"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/include/linux/nvmem-consumer.h b/include/linux/nvmem-consumer.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 34c0e58dfa26..5315bd862f5f 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/include/linux/nvmem-consumer.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/include/linux/nvmem-consumer.h"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@"},{"depth":1,"text":" #ifndef _LINUX_NVMEM_CONSUMER_H"},{"depth":1,"text":" #define _LINUX_NVMEM_CONSUMER_H"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+#include <linux/cleanup.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/err.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/errno.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/notifier.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -243,6 +244,8 @@ static inline struct nvmem_device *nvmem_device_find(void *data,"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" #endif /* CONFIG_NVMEM */"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+DEFINE_FREE(nvmem_cell_put, struct nvmem_cell *, if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(_T)) nvmem_cell_put(_T))"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":" #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NVMEM) && IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_OF)"},{"depth":1,"text":" struct nvmem_cell *of_nvmem_cell_get(struct device_node *np,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t     const char *id);"}],"lineCount":24,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260806074024.531259-3-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"},"20260815205457.6cd30d53@jic23-huawei":{"id":"20260815205457.6cd30d53@jic23-huawei","messageId":"20260815205457.6cd30d53@jic23-huawei","references":["20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com","20260806074024.531259-2-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260806074024.531259-2-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com","20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"],"author":{"name":"Jonathan Cameron","address":"jic23@kernel.org"},"sender":{"name":"linux-arm-kernel","address":"linux-arm-kernel-bounces@lists.infradead.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Varshini Rajendran","address":"varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"ehristev@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dlechner@baylibre.com"},{"name":"","address":"nuno.sa@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"andy@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"conor+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nicolas.ferre@microchip.com"},{"name":"","address":"alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com"},{"name":"","address":"claudiu.beznea@tuxon.dev"},{"name":"","address":"srini@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"marcelo.schmitt@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"radu.sabau@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"joshua.crofts1@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"jorge.marques@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"Jonathan.Santos@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"jishnu.prakash@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"duje@dujemihanovic.xyz"},{"name":"","address":"mazziesaccount@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-iio@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Krzysztof Kozlowski","address":"krzysztof.kozlowski@linaro.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-15T19:54:57.000Z","iso":"2026-08-15T19:54:57.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v6 01/17] dt-bindings: iio: adc: at91-sama5d2: document sama7d65","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","displayName":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:10:08 +0530\nVarshini Rajendran <varshini.rajendran@microchip.com> wrote:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Add dt-binding documentation for sama7d65 ADC."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"sama7d65 requires an individual compatible to address the differences"},{"depth":1,"text":"from its predecessor sama7g5. The main difference is the temperature"},{"depth":1,"text":"calibration layout and its handling."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Acked-by: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@linaro.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Varshini Rajendran <varshini.rajendran@microchip.com>"}],"lineCount":8,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi Varshini,"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"I'll probably tweak this when applying - but if for some reason\nanother version is needed please look at the ordering thing below."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/atmel,sama5d2-adc.yaml | 1 +"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/atmel,sama5d2-adc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/atmel,sama5d2-adc.yaml"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 4817b840977a..e8a65fdcd018 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/atmel,sama5d2-adc.yaml"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/atmel,sama5d2-adc.yaml"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ properties:"},{"depth":1,"text":"       - atmel,sama5d2-adc"},{"depth":1,"text":"       - microchip,sam9x60-adc"},{"depth":1,"text":"       - microchip,sama7g5-adc"},{"depth":1,"text":"+      - microchip,sama7d65-adc"}],"lineCount":13,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Alphabetical order."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"   reg:"},{"depth":1,"text":"     maxItems: 1"}],"lineCount":3,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260806074024.531259-2-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"},"20260815210018.460c0eca@jic23-huawei":{"id":"20260815210018.460c0eca@jic23-huawei","messageId":"20260815210018.460c0eca@jic23-huawei","references":["20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com","20260806074024.531259-5-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260806074024.531259-5-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com","20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"],"author":{"name":"Jonathan Cameron","address":"jic23@kernel.org"},"sender":{"name":"linux-arm-kernel","address":"linux-arm-kernel-bounces@lists.infradead.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Varshini Rajendran","address":"varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"ehristev@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dlechner@baylibre.com"},{"name":"","address":"nuno.sa@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"andy@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"conor+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nicolas.ferre@microchip.com"},{"name":"","address":"alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com"},{"name":"","address":"claudiu.beznea@tuxon.dev"},{"name":"","address":"srini@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"marcelo.schmitt@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"radu.sabau@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"joshua.crofts1@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"jorge.marques@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"Jonathan.Santos@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"jishnu.prakash@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"duje@dujemihanovic.xyz"},{"name":"","address":"mazziesaccount@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-iio@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-15T20:00:18.000Z","iso":"2026-08-15T20:00:18.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v6 04/17] iio: adc: at91-sama5d2_adc: rework temp calibration layout handling","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","displayName":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:10:11 +0530\nVarshini Rajendran <varshini.rajendran@microchip.com> wrote:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Extend support to handle different temperature calibration layouts."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Add a temperature calibration data layout structure to describe indexes"},{"depth":1,"text":"of the factors P1, P4, P6, tag, minimum length of the packet and the"},{"depth":1,"text":"scaling factors for P1 (p1_scale) which are SoC-specific instead of the"},{"depth":1,"text":"older non scalable id structure. This helps handle the differences in the"},{"depth":1,"text":"same function flow and prepare the calibration data to be applied."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Reviewed-by: Eugen Hristev <ehristev@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Varshini Rajendran <varshini.rajendran@microchip.com>"}],"lineCount":10,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"https://sashiko.dev/#/patchset/20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran%40microchip.com"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"For the unused define comment.  I 'might' tweak this is apply or go\nmeh i can't be bothered and apply it away :) \nAgain - if you respin for another reason please tidy this up."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The other comment from Sashiko doesn't seem particularly useful to\nme even if it is maybe valid."},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c | 66 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c b/drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 09390f082fc4..82db8f2f4db0 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/dmaengine.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/interrupt.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/io.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":"+#include <linux/math.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/module.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/platform_device.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/property.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -444,6 +445,27 @@ static const struct at91_adc_reg_layout sama7g5_layout = {"},{"depth":1,"text":" #define at91_adc_writel(st, reg, val)\t\t\t\t\t\\"},{"depth":1,"text":" \twritel_relaxed(val, (st)->base + (st)->soc_info.platform->layout->reg)"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+/* Temperature calibration tag \"ACST\" in ASCII */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+#define AT91_TEMP_CALIB_TAG_ACST\t0x41435354"}],"lineCount":22,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Eagle eyed sashiko spotted this isn't used in this patch.  Should have been\nintroduced with first use in patch 5 I think."}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":2,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260806074024.531259-5-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"},"20260815212113.65e60919@jic23-huawei":{"id":"20260815212113.65e60919@jic23-huawei","messageId":"20260815212113.65e60919@jic23-huawei","references":["20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com","20260806074024.531259-8-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260806074024.531259-8-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com","20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"],"author":{"name":"Jonathan Cameron","address":"jic23@kernel.org"},"sender":{"name":"linux-arm-kernel","address":"linux-arm-kernel-bounces@lists.infradead.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Varshini Rajendran","address":"varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"ehristev@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dlechner@baylibre.com"},{"name":"","address":"nuno.sa@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"andy@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"conor+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"nicolas.ferre@microchip.com"},{"name":"","address":"alexandre.belloni@bootlin.com"},{"name":"","address":"claudiu.beznea@tuxon.dev"},{"name":"","address":"srini@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"marcelo.schmitt@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"radu.sabau@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"joshua.crofts1@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"jorge.marques@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"Jonathan.Santos@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"jishnu.prakash@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"duje@dujemihanovic.xyz"},{"name":"","address":"mazziesaccount@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"linux-iio@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-15T20:21:13.000Z","iso":"2026-08-15T20:21:13.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v6 07/17] iio: adc: at91-sama5d2_adc: adapt the driver for sama7d65","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","displayName":"linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:10:14 +0530\nVarshini Rajendran <varshini.rajendran@microchip.com> wrote:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Add support for sama7d65 ADC. The differences are highlighted with the"},{"depth":1,"text":"compatible. The calibration data layout is the main difference."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Update Kconfig help text to mention SAMA7 SoC family support."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Varshini Rajendran <varshini.rajendran@microchip.com>"}],"lineCount":6,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The Sashiko feedback on this one is interesting."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"https://sashiko.dev/#/patchset/20260806074024.531259-1-varshini.rajendran%40microchip.com"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The timestamp in the chan_spec array isn't the last one - the\ntimestamp comes after it which is going to break in various\nunhelpful ways - as iio_push_to_buffers_with_timestamp() requires\nthe timestamp to be the last scan index."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"in at91_adc_trigger_handler_nodma() there is a comment saying\nthat it can only be used with voltage channels. That's fine but\nif they aren't useful, why are the scan_index values not -1\nwhich is how we hide those interfaces for channels for which\nbuffered capture is not supported."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Given you have the hardware set up, can you check if the\nscan_elements/*_en is there for the temp channel and\nthat for cases where it is enabled, we get an error in the\nbuffer preenable callback?"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"So I think it's a false positive but fair enough given the\ncurrent user interfaces seems likely to be rather odd."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Please sanity check all this."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"One other thing inline."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Jonathan"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/iio/adc/Kconfig            |  2 +-"},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++"},{"depth":1,"text":" 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/Kconfig b/drivers/iio/adc/Kconfig"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 3755a81c1efd..85b443853a08 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/iio/adc/Kconfig"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/Kconfig"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -647,7 +647,7 @@ config AT91_SAMA5D2_ADC"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tselect IIO_TRIGGERED_BUFFER"},{"depth":1,"text":" \thelp"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t  Say yes here to build support for Atmel SAMA5D2 ADC which is"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t  available on SAMA5D2 SoC family."},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t  available on SAMA5D2 and SAMA7 SoC families."},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" \t  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t  called at91-sama5d2_adc."},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c b/drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 3e9feb824a66..c1e5139a058c 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/at91-sama5d2_adc.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -528,6 +528,15 @@ static const struct at91_adc_temp_calib_layout sama7g5_temp_calib = {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t.p1_scale = { .numerator = 1000, .denominator = 1 },"},{"depth":1,"text":" };"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+static const struct at91_adc_temp_calib_layout sama7d65_temp_calib = {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.tag_idx = 1,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.p1_idx = 3,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.p4_idx = 2,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.p6_idx = 5,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.min_len = 11,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.p1_scale = { .numerator = 1, .denominator = 1000 },"},{"depth":1,"text":"+};"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":" /* Temperature sensor calibration - Vtemp voltage sensitivity to temperature. */"},{"depth":1,"text":" #define AT91_ADC_TS_VTEMP_DT\t\t(2080U)"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -766,6 +775,24 @@ static const struct at91_adc_platform sama7g5_platform = {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t.temp_calib_layout = &sama7g5_temp_calib,"},{"depth":1,"text":" };"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+static const struct at91_adc_platform sama7d65_platform = {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.layout = &sama7g5_layout,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.adc_channels = &at91_sama7g5_adc_channels,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.nr_channels = AT91_SAMA7G5_SINGLE_CHAN_CNT +"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t       AT91_SAMA7G5_DIFF_CHAN_CNT +"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t       AT91_SAMA7G5_TEMP_CHAN_CNT,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.max_channels = ARRAY_SIZE(at91_sama7g5_adc_channels),"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.max_index = AT91_SAMA7G5_MAX_CHAN_IDX,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.hw_trig_cnt = AT91_SAMA7G5_HW_TRIG_CNT,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.osr_mask = GENMASK(18, 16),"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.oversampling_avail = { 1, 4, 16, 64, 256 },"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.oversampling_avail_no = 5,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.chan_realbits = 16,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.temp_sensor = true,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.temp_chan = AT91_SAMA7G5_ADC_TEMP_CHANNEL,"}],"lineCount":57,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Is this ever used?"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"+\t.temp_calib_layout = &sama7d65_temp_calib,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+};"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":" static int at91_adc_chan_xlate(struct iio_dev *indio_dev, int chan)"},{"depth":1,"text":" {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tint i;"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -2632,6 +2659,9 @@ static const struct of_device_id at91_adc_dt_match[] = {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t}, {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t.compatible = \"microchip,sama7g5-adc\","},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t.data = &sama7g5_platform,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t}, {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t.compatible = \"microchip,sama7d65-adc\","},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t.data = &sama7d65_platform,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t}, {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t/* sentinel */"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t}"}],"lineCount":16,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":3,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260806074024.531259-8-varshini.rajendran@microchip.com"}},"rootIds":["20260815205238.6fbfb2f8@jic23-huawei","20260815205457.6cd30d53@jic23-huawei","20260815210018.460c0eca@jic23-huawei","20260815212113.65e60919@jic23-huawei"],"childrenByParent":{